      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we check `proc.poll()` after the sampling sleep and fail if VPP exited? `wait_for(marker, proc)` is the last liveness check; a VPP crash during the next two seconds leaves an unreaped zombie whose `/proc/PID/stat` remains readable and whose CPU time stops increasing, so this code prints PASS. I reproduced this with a local socket child that creates the EOF marker and then exits with status 42: the runner reported `cpu_cores\u003d0.000` and returned success. This would hide a crash in the EOF cleanup path.",
